-- The language a surface's own testimony was made in, read from provenance.
--
-- Consensus excludes source and context from identity (INVENTION §5), so the fold
-- cannot answer this; the attestation layer keeps it. context_id carries the
-- language for the lexical sources, and the row carries the fold's own inputs, so
-- the answer is an argmax over adjudicated evidence weight -- a row COUNT would be
-- the frequency prior §7 forbids.
--
-- Distinct from converse.word_language, which is an argmax over HAS_LANGUAGE
-- ASSERTIONS about the word. That form does not discriminate: a loanword carries
-- those edges in many languages at once. This reads which language the testimony
-- ITSELF came from, which is the question a language-scoped read is asking.
--
-- The set function owns that definition. This scalar is only a one-element adapter;
-- keeping another GROUP BY/argmax here previously made the documented "delegates"
-- contract false and let the two answers drift.
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION converse.attested_language(p_word bytea)
    RETURNS bytea
    LANGUAGE sql LAPLACE_STABLE_STRICT
BEGIN ATOMIC
    SELECT al.lang
    FROM converse.attested_language_batch(ARRAY[p_word]) al
    WHERE al.id = p_word;
END;
